{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","title":"def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.md","line":10,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.tex#def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.tex","label":"def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","line":17,"source":"\\begin{definition}[symmetric space]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0379}\n  A Riemannian manifold $(M,g)$ is \\emph{symmetric} if every $p\\in M$ admits\n  $A_p\\in\\mathrm{Iso}_p$ with $D_pA_p=-I$. This \\emph{point symmetry} reverses\n  each geodesic through $p$:\n  $A_p(c(t))=c(-t)$ whenever $c(0)=p$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[symmetric space] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d636831302d73796d6d65747269632d7370616365\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0379</span></span> A Riemannian manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> is <em>symmetric</em> if every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> admits <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A_p\\in \\mathrm{Iso}_p$\">$A_p\\in \\mathrm{Iso}_p$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D_pA_p=-I$\">$D_pA_p=-I$</span>. This <em>point symmetry</em> reverses each geodesic through <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>: <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$A_p(c(t))=c(-t)$\">$A_p(c(t))=c(-t)$</span> whenever <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c(0)=p$\">$c(0)=p$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#chap:pet-symmetric-spaces-and-holonomy","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#prop:pet-ch10-symmetric-homogeneous","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#prop:pet-ch10-symmetric-homogeneous","title":"prop:pet-ch10-symmetric-homogeneous","label":"prop:pet-ch10-symmetric-homogeneous"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#rem:pet-ch10-single-point-symmetry","title":"rem:pet-ch10-single-point-symmetry","label":"rem:pet-ch10-single-point-symmetry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#thm:pet-ch10-cartan-local-symmetry","title":"thm:pet-ch10-cartan-local-symmetry","label":"thm:pet-ch10-cartan-local-symmetry"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#thm:pet-ch10-cartan-isometry-extension","title":"thm:pet-ch10-cartan-isometry-extension","label":"thm:pet-ch10-cartan-isometry-extension"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy#def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","title":"def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space","tex":"\\begin{definition}[symmetric space]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch10-symmetric-space}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0379}\n  A Riemannian manifold $(M,g)$ is \\emph{symmetric} if every $p\\in M$ admits\n  $A_p\\in\\mathrm{Iso}_p$ with $D_pA_p=-I$. This \\emph{point symmetry} reverses\n  each geodesic through $p$:\n  $A_p(c(t))=c(-t)$ whenever $c(0)=p$.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch10_SymmetricSpacesAndHolonomy.tex","descri